Academic attribution
================================================================================

This plugin implements the technique described in the following paper, which
is independently licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(CC BY 4.0). The paper is the source of the underlying method; this codebase
is an independent implementation built from the paper.

  SketchVLM: Vision Language Models Can Annotate Images to Explain Thoughts
  and Guide Users
  Brandon Collins, Logan Bolton, Hung Huy Nguyen, Mohammad Reza Taesiri,
  Trung Bui, Anh Totti Nguyen.
  arXiv:2604.22875, 2026.
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.22875

  @misc{collins2026sketchvlmvisionlanguagemodels,
        title={SketchVLM: Vision language models can annotate images to
               explain thoughts and guide users},
        author={Brandon Collins and Logan Bolton and Hung Huy Nguyen and
                Mohammad Reza Taesiri and Trung Bui and Anh Totti Nguyen},
        year={2026},
        eprint={2604.22875},
        archivePrefix={arXiv},
        primaryClass={cs.CV},
